{"event": "Built docker exec command args=['docker', 'exec', '--workdir', '/workspace', '--user', '1000:1000', '--env', 'UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/uv-cache', '--env', 'PIP_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/pip-cache-dir', '--env', 'PIP_CONFIG_FILE=/tmp/pip-conf', '--env', 'HOME=/tmp/agent_home', '--env', 'CLAUDE_CODE_PRINT_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS=0', '--env', 'CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=***redacted***', '--env', 'FORCE_AUTO_BACKGROUND_TASKS=1', '--env', 'ENABLE_BACKGROUND_TASKS=1', '--env', 'CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_BETAS=1', '--env', 'DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=1', '--env', 'DISABLE_NON_ESSENTIAL_MODEL_CALLS=1', '--env', 'MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=31999', '--env', 'CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT_LEVEL=high', '--env', 'SLOP_EXEC_ID=0ca7dd3a806541b7b0c621be8e7e4b67', 'bdf85463c0d47283b091195f500f4f237cadd00efb0889e1b129a7587530580b', '/bin/sh', '-c', 'claude --output-format stream-json --verbose --model claude-opus-5 --disallowedTools Monitor --permission-mode bypassPermissions --print -- \\'# Task Directions\\n\\nFully implement the following spec. Use the approach:\\n- Environment setup\\n- Write tests from the spec\\n- Implement\\n- Declare complete\\n\\nSpecifically:\\n\\n# Environment\\n\\nKeep using the same virtual environment you started with, update `requirements.txt` with any new dependencies you need.\\nTouch an IN_PROGRESS file. Delete any COMPLETED file.\\n\\nWhen killing a process never run a pkill. Instead, pgrep.\\nMake sure only one process is found, then kill that one by PID.\\nWhy? It\\'\"\\'\"\\'s too easy to pkill your own Bash argv.\\n\\nFor long-lived processes, log to a file or /dev/null instead of an undrained pipe.\\n\\n# Testing\\n\\nSplit the spec file into minimal possible logical phrases and minimal context, and iterate through each phrase.\\nFor each phrase, add a test section with a comment of the phrase & context.\\n\\nIf the spec is non-trivially under-specified, such that alternative interpretations would change the behavior of a conforming implementation on some input, then never ask for clarification.\\nInstead, make your best choice at how to interpret the intention of the spec.\\nThen, add a numbered entry to an AMBIGUITIES.md file, starting with T1.\\nThe entry must have sections for Spec Text, Alternatives, Choice, and Risk.\\nThe entry will quote the relevant spec source verbatim, explain the reasonable alternative interpretations, and your choice & why it seems to best fit the spec.\\nThe \"### Risk: N\" section\\nRisk is a number from 0 to 100: the chance that the spec\\'\"\\'\"\\'s author, who has an implementation of their own and writes the hidden tests against it, prefers a different reading from your choice on some tested input.\\nReason about what the author\\'\"\\'\"\\'s implementation most likely does and what fixture they would naturally write, not only about which reading the prose supports best.\\nIf Risk is above 0, name the reading the author most likely prefers in one line.\\nUse the whole range: a flat number on every entry is useless.\\n\\nIf a previous ambiguity is resolved by the current spec, annotate the entry instead of removing it.\\n\\nYou run tests only to validate the tests themselves: collection succeeds, helpers and generators work, and each failure is because behavior is missing, not because the test is broken. Quick, targeted runs.\\n\\nNever run the full suite to completion or long hypothesis runs; a green suite is the implementer\\'\"\\'\"\\'s job, not yours.\\n\\n# Implement\\n# Declare complete\\n\\ntouch a COMPLETED file. rm the IN_PROGRESS file.\\n\\n# Spec\\n## Optional Dataset Enrichment\\n\\n`/convert` supports optional ingestion enrichment with `enrich=yes`.\\n\\n### Enrichment trigger\\n\\nOnly a single, exact `enrich=yes` enables enrichment.\\nAll other states keep enrichment off.\\nSuccess response remains:\\n\\n```json\\n{\"ok\": true, \"endpoint\": \"/datasets/<id>\"}\\n```\\n\\n### Enriched query output\\n\\nFor enriched CSV datasets, add:\\n\\n- `dataset_summary` with at least `filetype`, `row_count`, `column_count`\\n- `column_details` keyed by column name with at least `type`, `distinct_count`, `missing_count`\\n\\nType labels: `text`, `number`, `integer`, `float`.\\n\\nFor enriched spreadsheet datasets, add only `dataset_summary` with `filetype: \"excel\"`.\\n\\nNon-enriched responses omit both metadata fields (no `null`/empty objects).\\n`rows`, `columns`, `ok`, `query_ms`, and `total` do not change.\\n\\n### Cache and enrichment\\n\\n- `enrich=yes` on a cached non-enriched dataset forces re-ingestion and upgrades stored state.\\n- `enrich=yes` on a cached enriched dataset may use cache.\\n- Requests without re-ingestion do not change stored enrichment state.\\n- Re-ingestion recomputes metadata from current source bytes.\\n- `enrich` applies only on `/convert`.\\n\\n### Error handling\\n\\nEnrichment failures return standard JSON errors and must not downgrade to non-enriched storage.\\'']", "timestamp": "2026-09-15 02:45:10", "level": "verbose", "process_id": 321215, "thread_name": "MainThread"}
